<GuideLayout
  title="Eco-Performance Fabric Trends for Activewear Brands"
  type="FABRIC TREND REPORT"
  description="A practical guide to eco-performance fabric trends including recycled nylon, recycled polyester, bio-based yarns and durability testing for activewear brands."
>
  <p>Sustainable activewear is moving from marketing language to material performance. Buyers now ask whether recycled or lower-impact fabrics can still deliver stretch recovery, squat-proof coverage, moisture management and long wash durability.</p>

  <h2>Important Fabric Directions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Recycled nylon for premium hand feel and compression.</li>
    <li>Recycled polyester for gym wear, training tops and quick-dry styles.</li>
    <li>Bio-based yarn blends for brands testing new sustainability stories.</li>
    <li>Solution-dyed and low-water dyeing options for selected programs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What Buyers Should Verify</h2>
  <p>Eco claims should be backed by fabric documentation, composition details, colorfastness tests and real garment samples. A fabric that looks sustainable on paper still needs to pass opacity, pilling, shrinkage and stretch recovery checks.</p>

  <h2>Fitclo Recommendation</h2>
  <p>For first launches, choose one or two eco-performance fabrics and test them across a focused product group. This reduces inventory risk while giving your brand a credible sustainability direction.</p>
</GuideLayout>
